## TLDR Problem this solves: - Bedrock managed batches could not be cancelled through the proxy - `POST /v1/batches/{id}/cancel` returned 400 without reaching AWS - The Bedrock job kept running and billing to completion How it solves it: - Batch cancel now calls Bedrock `StopModelInvocationJob` - Returns the refreshed job status after stopping - Maps `Stopping` to `cancelling` and `Stopped` to `cancelled` - Cancelling an already finished job returns its terminal status - Genuine stop failures still raise instead of being swallowed ## User Flow Before: the cancel call is rejected by the gateway, and the Bedrock job keeps running and billing to completion 1. An operator uploads a 100-record JSONL with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files (multipart: `purpose=batch`, `target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku`, the file) and gets back a long scrambled managed file id 2. They start the batch with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches sending `{"input_file_id": "<that id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}` and get a batch id with `"status": "validating"` 3. They realize the batch was submitted by mistake and call POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel 4. The call fails with HTTP 400: `LiteLLM doesn't support bedrock for 'cancel_batch'. Only 'openai', 'azure', and 'vertex_ai' are supported.` 5. GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} keeps showing `"status": "in_progress"` until the job finishes, and every record is billed After: the same cancel call stops the job at AWS, and the batch reports cancelling, then cancelled 1. An operator uploads a 100-record JSONL with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/files (multipart: `purpose=batch`, `target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku`, the file) and gets back a long scrambled managed file id 2. They start the batch with POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches sending `{"input_file_id": "<that id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}` and get a batch id with `"status": "validating"` 3. They realize the batch was submitted by mistake and call POST https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel 4. The call returns HTTP 200 with the batch showing `"status": "cancelling"` 5. GET https://litellm-domain/v1/batches/{batch_id} soon shows `"status": "cancelled"`, and the job has stopped at AWS ## Relevant issues Fixes #33986 ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-4854 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Live proxy plus real AWS Bedrock model invocation jobs (us-west-2, `bedrock/us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`, managed file with `target_model_names`), no mocks. Each leg uploads a 100-record JSONL, creates a batch, then cancels it through the proxy ### Before, at base `91aee78e78`: cancel is rejected and the AWS job keeps running ``` $ curl -sS http://localhost:41837/v1/files -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -F purpose=batch -F target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku -F file=@batch_input.jsonl {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTphcHBsaWNhdGlvbi9vY3RldC1zdHJlYW07...NGIzNw","object":"file","purpose":"batch","status":"uploaded",...} $ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:41837/v1/batches -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"input_file_id": "<file_id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}' {"id":"<unified_batch_id>","object":"batch","status":"validating",...} $ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:41837/v1/batches/<batch_id>/cancel \ -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" {"error":{"message":"litellm.BadRequestError: LiteLLM doesn't support bedrock for 'cancel_batch'. Only 'openai', 'azure', and 'vertex_ai' are supported....","type":"internal_server_error","param":null,"code":"400"}} HTTP 400 $ curl -sS http://localhost:41837/v1/batches/<batch_id> -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" {"id":"<unified_batch_id>","object":"batch","status":"validating","cancelling_at":null,"cancelled_at":null,...} $ aws bedrock list-model-invocation-jobs --region us-west-2 --max-results 5 --sort-by CreationTime --sort-order Descending \ --query 'invocationJobSummaries[0].[jobArn,status]' [ "arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2:...:model-invocation-job/bbp12ydc1e3w", "Submitted" ] ``` The orphaned provider job had to be stopped out of band with `aws bedrock stop-model-invocation-job` ### After, at PR head `4114f907ea`: the same cancel stops the AWS job ``` $ curl -sS http://localhost:41387/v1/files -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -F purpose=batch -F target_model_names=bedrock-batch-haiku -F file=@batch_input.jsonl {"id":"bGl0ZWxsbV9wcm94eTphcHBsaWNhdGlvbi9vY3RldC1zdHJlYW07...","object":"file","purpose":"batch","status":"uploaded",...} $ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:41387/v1/batches -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" \ -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"input_file_id": "<file_id>", "endpoint": "/v1/chat/completions", "completion_window": "24h"}' {"id":"<unified_batch_id>","object":"batch","status":"validating",...} $ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:41387/v1/batches/<batch_id>/cancel \ -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" {"id":"<unified_batch_id>","object":"batch","status":"cancelling",...,"metadata":{...,"job_arn":"arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2:...:model-invocation-job/12lktui6n5r6",...}} HTTP 200 $ curl -sS http://localhost:41387/v1/batches/<batch_id> -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-qa-***" {"id":"<unified_batch_id>","object":"batch","status":"cancelled",...} $ aws bedrock list-model-invocation-jobs --region us-west-2 --max-results 5 --sort-by CreationTime --sort-order Descending \ --query 'invocationJobSummaries[0].[jobArn,status]' [ "arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2:...:model-invocation-job/12lktui6n5r6", "Stopped" ] ``` No out-of-band cleanup was needed: the proxy's cancel alone drove the Bedrock job to `Stopped` within seconds QA observations, not caused by this PR: - Cancelled batch retrieve leaves `cancelled_at` null; mapping predates PR - Batch retrieve shows `request_counts` total 0; predates PR - Before-leg 400 body says `internal_server_error`; path removed by PR ## Type 🐛 Bug Fix ## Caveats (if any) ### Final Attestation - [x] The tests check the right things, including the edge cases, and regressions in the respective real-world customer use-cases are not possible after this PR

## TLDR Problem this solves: - `fireworks_ai/<slug>` always expands to `accounts/fireworks/models/<slug>`, so Fireworks routers 404 on short slugs - Only workaround is the full id `fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/routers/<id>`, which most users do not know - Chat and text-completion transforms had drifted: chat had a `-fast` router branch, text completion did not How it solves it: - Add shared `resolve_fireworks_resource_name` helper mapping `routers/<id>` and `models/<id>` onto `accounts/fireworks/...` - Keeps the `-fast` router heuristic and defaults bare slugs to `models/`, so existing configs keep working - Both chat and text-completion transforms call it, so the two paths cannot drift again ## User Flow Before: a developer whose traffic goes through a Fireworks router gets 404s unless they know the full resource path 1. The proxy admin configures a deployment with `model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest` and starts the proxy 2. A developer sends POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "fw-glm-latest"` 3. They get back HTTP 404 with "Model not found, inaccessible, and/or not deployed", the same answer Fireworks gives for a model that does not exist 4. POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions, POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages, and POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses against the same deployment fail with the same 404 5. The only fix is rewriting the config to the full `fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/routers/glm-latest` id After: the same short config reaches the router and returns completions 1. The proxy admin configures a deployment with `model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest` and starts the proxy 2. A developer sends POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "fw-glm-latest"` 3. They get HTTP 200 with a completion from whichever model the Fireworks router selected 4. POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions, POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages, and POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses against the same deployment also return 200 5. Existing configs using bare slugs like `fireworks_ai/glm-5p2` still resolve to `accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p2` and keep working unchanged ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5294 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix QA run over the User Flow with a live proxy per commit, no DB, hitting the real Fireworks AI API. Both legs boot the same config on a random free port and drive the same curls in the same order, six seconds apart so the default five second cooldown after a failed call never masks the next surface ```yaml model_list: - model_name: fw-glm-latest litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest api_key: os.environ/FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY - model_name: fw-glm-5p2 litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/glm-5p2 api_key: os.environ/FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: sk-1234 ``` Booted with `python litellm/proxy/proxy_cli.py --config config.yaml --port PORT`, then: ### Before, at merge base 3840970613 (litellm_internal_staging tip): every router-slug surface 404s, bare slug works chat completions via router slug ``` $ curl -s -w "
