## TLDR Problem this solves: - `fireworks_ai/<slug>` always expands to `accounts/fireworks/models/<slug>`, so Fireworks routers 404 on short slugs - Only workaround is the full id `fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/routers/<id>`, which most users do not know - Chat and text-completion transforms had drifted: chat had a `-fast` router branch, text completion did not How it solves it: - Add shared `resolve_fireworks_resource_name` helper mapping `routers/<id>` and `models/<id>` onto `accounts/fireworks/...` - Keeps the `-fast` router heuristic and defaults bare slugs to `models/`, so existing configs keep working - Both chat and text-completion transforms call it, so the two paths cannot drift again ## User Flow Before: a developer whose traffic goes through a Fireworks router gets 404s unless they know the full resource path 1. The proxy admin configures a deployment with `model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest` and starts the proxy 2. A developer sends POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "fw-glm-latest"` 3. They get back HTTP 404 with "Model not found, inaccessible, and/or not deployed", the same answer Fireworks gives for a model that does not exist 4. POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions, POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages, and POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses against the same deployment fail with the same 404 5. The only fix is rewriting the config to the full `fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/routers/glm-latest` id After: the same short config reaches the router and returns completions 1. The proxy admin configures a deployment with `model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest` and starts the proxy 2. A developer sends POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "fw-glm-latest"` 3. They get HTTP 200 with a completion from whichever model the Fireworks router selected 4. POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions, POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages, and POST https://litellm-domain/v1/responses against the same deployment also return 200 5. Existing configs using bare slugs like `fireworks_ai/glm-5p2` still resolve to `accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p2` and keep working unchanged ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5294 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix QA run over the User Flow with a live proxy per commit, no DB, hitting the real Fireworks AI API. Both legs boot the same config on a random free port and drive the same curls in the same order, six seconds apart so the default five second cooldown after a failed call never masks the next surface ```yaml model_list: - model_name: fw-glm-latest litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/routers/glm-latest api_key: os.environ/FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY - model_name: fw-glm-5p2 litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/glm-5p2 api_key: os.environ/FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY general_settings: master_key: sk-1234 ``` Booted with `python litellm/proxy/proxy_cli.py --config config.yaml --port PORT`, then: ### Before, at merge base 3840970613 (litellm_internal_staging tip): every router-slug surface 404s, bare slug works chat completions via router slug ``` $ curl -s -w "
